nal inquiry","title":"Implementation of 1988 BCO amendments on Assistant Pastors","year":1989,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga17_1989__ci03.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga17_1989__ci03.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:13-3--inquiry:inquiries/ga17_1989__ci03.md:occ-156a7715cd4f","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga17_1989__ci03.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga17_1989__ci03.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["index/inquiries_search.json:provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga17_1989__ci03.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"summary":"Tennessee Valley Presbytery asked whether the new BCO 22-3/22-4 Assistant Pastor provisions applied retroactively, to all full-time ministers, and whether a lesser examination was appropriate."}},{"id":"bco:13-3--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Psiaki v. Pacific Northwest Presbytery","year":2024,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:13-3--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md:occ-9d775bfb0fec","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":345},"excerpt":"…entrusted solely to that institution rather than to the Assembly. Or consider BCO 13-3 which states that every ruling elder not known to the Presbytery shall produce a certificate of his “regular appointment\" from the Session of the church whom he…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["minor communicant voting","congregational meeting","voting rights","good and regular standing","church bylaws","officer election","communicant membership","BCO 6-4","BCO 20-3","BCO 24-3","BCO 25-1","age restrictions","session authority"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2023-11"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"The SJC sustained Psiaki’s complaint and held that the CPC Session erred by ordaining and installing officers elected at a February 5, 2023 congregational meeting where the congregation’s bylaw excluded communing members under 18 from voting. Reading BCO 6-4, 25-1, and 25-7 together, the SJC ruled that all communing members are entitled to vote and that local bylaws cannot impose an age restriction; the “good and regular standing” language addresses censure, not age. The decision did not annul the completed ordination/installation, but required future elections and installations to comply with the Constitution."}},{"id":"bco:13-3--case:cases/ga36_2008__2007-14.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga36_2008__2007-14.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"PCA v. Louisiana Presbytery (Trial)","year":2008,"disposition":"dismissed","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga36_2008__2007-14.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga36_2008__2007-14.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:13-3--case:cases/ga36_2008__2007-14.md:occ-198e07fe6f78","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga36_2008__2007-14.html","repository_path":"cases/ga36_2008__2007-14.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":180},"excerpt":"procedures of a judicial commission as described in BCO 15-3. BCO 13-3","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga36_2008__2007-14.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"standard_of_review":"important_delinquency_or_grossly_unconstitutional_proceeding","review_standards":["important_delinquency_or_grossly_unconstitutional_proceeding"],"case_numbers":["2007-14"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"In this BCO 40-5 proceeding over Louisiana Presbytery’s investigation of TE Stephen Wilkins, the SJC dismissed Specification 1 because it could not find that the cited procedures were constitutionally required or that guilt was proved. The dismissal did not erase concerns about undocumented doctrinal findings; those failures were covered by Specification 2. On Presbytery’s guilty plea to that specification, the SJC imposed a public admonition for failing to find a strong presumption of doctrinal guilt and pursue trial. Wilkins’s and his church’s withdrawal made practical amends unavailable."}},{"id":"bco:13-3--overture:ga16_1988:11","record_id":"overture:ga16_1988:11","type":"Overture","title":"Amend BCO 13-2 and Add BCO 13-3 to Create Appendix Roll for Uncalled Teaching Elders","year":1988,"disposition":"","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga16_1988.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga16_1988.md","evidence_basis":"overture_action_target","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:13-3--overture:ga16_1988:11:occ-38b7a4ffa206","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga16_1988.html#ga16-p59","repository_path":"markdown/ga16_1988.md#ga16-p59","locator":{"fragment":"ga16-p59","page":59}